/*

OOEntityObjectNamesTable.h

The names a C++ entity's Objective-C object (the root's facade, class Entity) answered outside the
by-name table OOEntityCalledByNameTable.h (bead oo-9ht.39.9, ADR-0056 amendment oo-9ht.39.9):
measured on main 0836d09a6 by asking the facade of a ship, a station, a dock, the player, a proxy,
a visual effect and a waypoint each name of its class and its root classes, with OOCallByName's
rules (a planet's five shader names from their declarations). This file is the source (the facade
it was proved equal to went with bead oo-dpyk8).

One row per name: when the object answered it (null: every entity; the planet's and the beacon's
names for the parts the facade's -respondsToSelector: answered them for), the kind (OOEntityCalledByName.h)
and the method's type encoding, as OOCallByName logged it. The JS glue the facade no longer answers
(isVisibleToScripts, deleteJSSelf; bead oo-9ht.39.8.9) has no row: a call to it does not respond.
Included by OOEntityCalledByName.mm only, after AnswersPlanet() and AnswersBeacon().

*/

